msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ascii-video_SKILL.md:8
msgid "Creative Standard"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ascii-video_SKILL.md:10
msgid ""
"This is visual art. ASCII characters are the medium; cinema is the "
"standard."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ascii-video_SKILL.md:12
msgid ""
"**Before writing a single line of code**, articulate the creative "
"concept. What is the mood? What visual story does this tell? What makes "
"THIS project different from every other ASCII video? The user's prompt is"
" a starting point — interpret it with creative ambition, not literal "
"transcription."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ascii-video_SKILL.md:14
msgid ""
"**First-render excellence is non-negotiable.** The output must be "
"visually striking without requiring revision rounds. If something looks "
"generic, flat, or like \"AI-generated ASCII art,\" it is wrong — rethink "
"the creative concept before shipping."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ascii-video_SKILL.md:16
msgid ""
"**Go beyond the reference vocabulary.** The effect catalogs, shader "
"presets, and palette libraries in the references are a starting "
"vocabulary. For every project, combine, modify, and invent new patterns. "
"The catalog is a palette of paints — you write the painting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ascii-video_SKILL.md:18
msgid ""
"**Be proactively creative.** Extend the skill's vocabulary when the "
"project calls for it. If the references don't have what the vision "
"demands, build it. Include at least one visual moment the user didn't ask"
" for but will appreciate — a transition, an effect, a color choice that "
"elevates the whole piece."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ascii-video_SKILL.md:20
msgid ""
"**Cohesive aesthetic over technical correctness.** All scenes in a video "
"must feel connected by a unifying visual language — shared color "
"temperature, related character palettes, consistent motion vocabulary. A "
"technically correct video where every scene uses a random different "
"effect is an aesthetic failure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ascii-video_SKILL.md:22
msgid ""
"**Dense, layered, considered.** Every frame should reward viewing. Never "
"flat black backgrounds. Always multi-grid composition. Always per-scene "
"variation. Always intentional color."
msgstr ""

